    "narrative": "Our core lineup for July 17th is anchored by **Tyler Freeman** (64.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.78), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Tyler Freeman** is a high-upside play today; despite batting 8th, his projection is buoyed by an elite park factor and a solid matchup against Singer. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s position at the top of the order provides the stability we need in 5x5 scoring, as his efficiency is boosted by his role in setting the table for the heart of the order. **Masyn Winn** (61.81) and **Lawrence Butler** (60.69) also clear the 60-point threshold comfortably, with **Lawrence Butler** standing out as a premier play due to his 13% platoon edge against Cavalli, a matchup that creates significant potential for power-speed production.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Dylan Beavers** (59.04), whose score is uniquely inflated by a 4% bump for the aggressive \"slow delivery\" status of his opposing pitcher, increasing his stolen base floor\u2014a critical factor for our roster construction. The most difficult bench decision involved **Luis Arraez**, who posted a 44.52 score; while his contact profile is enticing, the brutal matchup against Miller (2.85 xERA) suppressed his ceiling enough to keep him on the pine in favor of the higher-efficiency profiles of **Gavin Sheets** and **Daulton Varsho**. We are navigating some risk with **Cal Raleigh** (53.78) and **Jonathan Aranda** (47.18), both of whom are facing difficult left-handed arms or unfavorable platoon splits, though their raw power keeps them in the lineup over our bench depth. We currently have no weather concerns, but owners should note that **Bryce Harper** remains sidelined today due to the team\u2019s scheduled off-day.",
